      "text": "GM to those who keep grinding. Here is your daily Market Movers (03.11):\n\nCRYPTO ROUNDUP\n\n₿ $BTC stuck at $69.5K, couldn't hold $71K Tuesday as war uncertainty kept risk appetite in check. Fear & Greed at 25, up from last month's Extreme Fear but still firmly in Fear territory.\n\n📊 $BTC ETFs saw $167M net inflow on Mar 9, BlackRock leading. $ETH, $XRP, $SOL ETFs all posted outflows same day, suggesting narrow institutional demand.\n\n⚡ Strategy (fka MicroStrategy) bought 17,994 $BTC for $1.28B between Mar 2-8 at avg $70,946. Total holdings now 738,731 BTC. Saylor buying the war dip.\n\n🔵 $DOT Polkadot spot ETF (ticker TDOT) now live on Nasdaq, with a hard catalyst March 12: a major economic upgrade cutting emissions 53.6% and capping supply.\n\nAI & TECH\n\n🤖 $ORCL exploded 13.8% on earnings, raised FY2027 sales guidance to $90B. Revenue $17.19B, up 18%, beat by $270M. Cloud up 41%. Management called SaaS apocalypse fears overblown, says AI agents will strengthen platforms, not cannibalize them.\n\n🤖 Apple's rebuilt Siri targeting March 2026 release with iOS 26.4, powered by Google's Gemini 1.2T parameter model via Private Cloud Compute. The AI assistant wars are heating up.\n\n🤖 IRGC released a list of top US companies with Israeli links whose tech has been used militarily. $NVDA, defense/AI chip supply chains on watch if list triggers secondary sanctions pressure.\n\nFINANCE & INVESTMENT\n\n📉 Feb CPI: +2.4% YoY, +0.3% MoM, in line with forecasts. Core CPI +2.5% YoY, unchanged from Jan. The report predates the Iran oil shock entirely, so Mar CPI will be the real test.\n\n📉 $SPX flat to slightly positive in early trade. $ORCL rally lifted Nasdaq (+0.3%), $NVDA edging higher. $GOLD pulling back to $5,181 from $5,219 yesterday as energy fears ease slightly.\n\n⚠️ Feb jobs report shed 92,000 jobs vs. expectations of +58,000 added. Unemployment 4.4%. Worst monthly reading since 2020. Stagflation risk rising as energy shock hits into a weakening jobs market.\n\n🏦 Fed March 18 decision: markets pricing 100% hold. No cuts through April now consensus. Warsh confirmation as Fed Chair looming as a major variable for H2 rate trajectory.\n\nGEOPOLITICS\n\n🇺🇸🇮🇱🇮🇷 Day 12 of Operation Epic Fury. Hegseth called today \"our most intense day of strikes yet\" with the most fighters, bombers, and strikes deployed so far.\n\n🇮🇷 Iran says nearly 10,000 civilian sites bombed, 1,300+ civilians killed. Internet blackout at 240 hours, among the longest state-imposed shutdowns on record globally.\n\n🇮🇷🇦🇪 UAE refinery hit by Iran drone strike, fire reported. 85 countries have now reported petrol price rises since Feb 28. Manila introducing 4-day work week in response to fuel costs.\n\n🇱🇧 Israel began ground raids into southern Lebanon, weighing deeper push. Hezbollah front reopening alongside Iran conflict. Second front expanding.",
